(1894456, 260703, 39850, '<td valign="top">5 - Mostly for the potential.  Criticism; needs to be at least 640 (width in this case).  The heavy top/bottom frame detracts in my opinion.  This is a good shot with a seemingly nice background effect with the reflection off the water, but you lost a lot in the resizing (possibly also quality issues too(?) - seems to be noise/grain, not sure).  Like the ''composition'' and the colors, ''if only'' the seedheads were a touch sharper, and maybe the ''tallest'' stem not ''blown'' (but then that does add a different effect here that could be used/incorporated), may have made this a better shot in my opinion.</td>', '5 - Mostly for the potential.  Criticism; needs to be at least 640 (width in this case).  The heavy top/bottom frame detracts in my opinion.  This is a good shot with a seemingly nice background effect with the reflection off the water, but you lost a lot in the resizing (possibly also quality issues too(?) - seems to be noise/grain, not sure).  Like the ''composition'' and the colors, ''if only'' the seedheads were a touch sharper, and maybe the ''tallest'' stem not ''blown'' (but then that does add a different effect here that could be used/incorporated), may have made this a better shot in my opinion.', '2005-11-23 23:44:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1894467, 261118, 39850, '<td valign="top">7 - Good and ''odd'', I am sure the size restrictions don''t do this justice.  Criticism; want to say wish there was some sharpness around the edge of what looks like glass beads(?), but then you''d likely lose the focus on the refractions, so who knows.  Nice colors and although the refraction idea is obviously not ''new'', the multiple in almost symmetry may be yours, if so, well done.  Maybe a slightly different crop on this, or ''composition'' (if possible), especially to gain more ''symmetry'', may have made this better in my opinion.</td>', '7 - Good and ''odd'', I am sure the size restrictions don''t do this justice.  Criticism; want to say wish there was some sharpness around the edge of what looks like glass beads(?), but then you''d likely lose the focus on the refractions, so who knows.  Nice colors and although the refraction idea is obviously not ''new'', the multiple in almost symmetry may be yours, if so, well done.  Maybe a slightly different crop on this, or ''composition'' (if possible), especially to gain more ''symmetry'', may have made this better in my opinion.', '2005-11-23 23:48:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1894477, 261161, 39850, '<td valign="top">8 - Wow!  Echium ((?) Pride of Madeira).. excellent angle/perspective and detail, colors.  Criticism; not much, maybe the sky blow out issues, but difficult as you captured the tips very well, and still retained the ''height'' context/perspective.  Perhaps just a little more focus &amp;/or ''blue'' on the actual flowers, but difficult, and you certainly captured the foliage quite well - although I know it to be slightly more gray/green.  Taking the liberty and putting into Favorites.  Apt title.</td>', '8 - Wow!  Echium ((?) Pride of Madeira).. excellent angle/perspective and detail, colors.  Criticism; not much, maybe the sky blow out issues, but difficult as you captured the tips very well, and still retained the ''height'' context/perspective.  Perhaps just a little more focus &/or ''blue'' on the actual flowers, but difficult, and you certainly captured the foliage quite well - although I know it to be slightly more gray/green.  Taking the liberty and putting into Favorites.  Apt title.', '2005-11-23 23:56:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1894491, 261132, 39850, '<td valign="top">8 - Very nice.  Good color control.   Criticism; not much, maybe slightly more ''dramatic'' lighting and more symmetry top left corner where the two stems are ''appearing'', may have made this even better in my opinion.  Seems a little ''spot'' below the left calla, pixelish, who knows.</td>', '8 - Very nice.  Good color control.   Criticism; not much, maybe slightly more ''dramatic'' lighting and more symmetry top left corner where the two stems are ''appearing'', may have made this even better in my opinion.  Seems a little ''spot'' below the left calla, pixelish, who knows.', '2005-11-24 00:05:59.000000', NULL, 1),
