(1906758, 260908, 45559, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your wonderful comments(23 so far my personal best) and let me tell you how this photo was made(yep,in basic editing):<br/> <br/>   First of all I took a last year photo made on film at the seaside of the Black Sea. Using the scissors and a cutter I cuted out myself very precisely, takeing care of the little details as u can see.<br/>   Then comes the egg part:I cracked an egg,emptyed the content,cleaned it and finaly fixed the cutout in the shell.The rest is history.Just set up the shot finding the best ligth direction for the shadow effect.<br/>   PhotoshopCS2 edit: autolevels,brightness set to +10,contrast set to +5,cropped,resized,saved for web,after that applied neat image plugin and final save.<br/> <br/>Thank u all again.....still looking forward to break the top 10 though.<br/> <br/>   George.</td>', 'Thank you all for your wonderful comments(23 so far my personal best) and let me tell you how this photo was made(yep,in basic editing):    First of all I took a last year photo made on film at the seaside of the Black Sea. Using the scissors and a cutter I cuted out myself very precisely, takeing care of the little details as u can see.   Then comes the egg part:I cracked an egg,emptyed the content,cleaned it and finaly fixed the cutout in the shell.The rest is history.Just set up the shot finding the best ligth direction for the shadow effect.   PhotoshopCS2 edit: autolevels,brightness set to +10,contrast set to +5,cropped,resized,saved for web,after that applied neat image plugin and final save. Thank u all again.....still looking forward to break the top 10 though.    George.', '2005-11-30 04:53:38.000000', NULL, 0);
