(1906763, 261016, 27812, '<td valign="top">great moment and so well presented. sorry it did not fare better.</td>', 'great moment and so well presented. sorry it did not fare better.', '2005-11-30 04:59:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1906764, 260883, 16493, '<td valign="top">Congratilations on your first blue ribbon.</td>', 'Congratilations on your first blue ribbon.', '2005-11-30 05:00:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1906765, 260883, 28750, '<td valign="top">Til hamingju með 1 sætið</td>', 'Til hamingju með 1 sætið', '2005-11-30 05:00:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(1906782, 260851, 31889, '<td valign="top">Love it.....well done on 4th spot.</td>', 'Love it.....well done on 4th spot.', '2005-11-30 05:25:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1906794, 260662, 4281, '<td valign="top">An extremely funny and creative photo and my favorite in the challenge. <br/>I love how the swan seems to be ''communicating'' or dancing for the cone. <br/>I''m also fond of the gradient which emphasises the difference between the swan and the cone. It''s also illustrative how you''ve placed the cone and the bird at distance in the frame to emphasise that these two will always be apart despite the obvious affection between them!<br/>All in all, a truly neat picture and it''s funny how cone seems to be smirking because of the swan''s misunderstanding (it looks like the cone has a mouth).<br/> <br/>Nitpicking, I find the cone to be overexposed in the red channel. Perhaps it would be wise to tone down the red slightly to get more detail out of it.<br/> <br/>And congratulations on the ribbon!</td>', 'An extremely funny and creative photo and my favorite in the challenge. I love how the swan seems to be ''communicating'' or dancing for the cone. I''m also fond of the gradient which emphasises the difference between the swan and the cone. It''s also illustrative how you''ve placed the cone and the bird at distance in the frame to emphasise that these two will always be apart despite the obvious affection between them!All in all, a truly neat picture and it''s funny how cone seems to be smirking because of the swan''s misunderstanding (it looks like the cone has a mouth). Nitpicking, I find the cone to be overexposed in the red channel. Perhaps it would be wise to tone down the red slightly to get more detail out of it. And congratulations on the ribbon!', '2005-11-30 05:36:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(1906795, 260883, 27482, '<td valign="top">Congrats on another ribbon, I got to step up my game before you overtake me in the ribbon race, 2 in 19 challenges, that´s not too shabby :D<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-11-30 05:36:38.</i></td>', 'Congrats on another ribbon, I got to step up my game before you overtake me in the ribbon race, 2 in 19 challenges, that´s not too shabby :D', '2005-11-30 05:36:23.000000', '2005-11-30 05:36:38.000000', 0),
(1906803, 260013, 42198, '<td valign="top">Excellent! - Should have got the blue though :)<br/> <br/>One of the best images I''ve seen in a long time. Composition is spot on. Evocative, and very beautiful.</td>', 'Excellent! - Should have got the blue though :) One of the best images I''ve seen in a long time. Composition is spot on. Evocative, and very beautiful.', '2005-11-30 05:40:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(1906805, 260662, 41746, '<td valign="top">Glad to be the other one that gave you 9. Brilliant... and the title perfect. Congrats!</td>', 'Glad to be the other one that gave you 9. Brilliant... and the title perfect. Congrats!', '2005-11-30 05:42:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1906812, 259110, 47310, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for the nice comments! I am really happy you liked my photo.<br/>I wanted it to be different from the things people usually shoot, that is why I chose the odd angle. The yellowish light that makes the colours of the three and the building so lively/saturated was coming from a neabry lamp. It made a good \"filling\" to the image which would not have been nearly as vivid with only the moon as a light source. <br/> <br/>Thanks again!</td>', 'Thank you all for the nice comments! I am really happy you liked my photo.I wanted it to be different from the things people usually shoot, that is why I chose the odd angle. The yellowish light that makes the colours of the three and the building so lively/saturated was coming from a neabry lamp. It made a good \"filling\" to the image which would not have been nearly as vivid with only the moon as a light source.  Thanks again!', '2005-11-30 05:52:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1906816, 260851, 27482, '<td valign="top">Very good, close but I figure you will get there in the end, I smell a ribbon in your future, no question (especially since you just recently started using "L glass")<br/> <br/>:D</td>', 'Very good, close but I figure you will get there in the end, I smell a ribbon in your future, no question (especially since you just recently started using "L glass") :D', '2005-11-30 05:57:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1906829, 261132, 23394, '<td valign="top">very nicely crafted!  it is so cool, what you are able to get out of your camera.  and to think you do this with challenges in mind, under basic editing constraints--very inspiring to me, and i should hope to others.</td>', 'very nicely crafted!  it is so cool, what you are able to get out of your camera.  and to think you do this with challenges in mind, under basic editing constraints--very inspiring to me, and i should hope to others.', '2005-11-30 06:18:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1906895, 260883, 34956, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments votes and my first blue ribbon :-) Takk takk</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments votes and my first blue ribbon :-) Takk takk', '2005-11-30 07:27:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(1906899, 259399, 44728, '<td valign="top">Thanks, wish more people thougth/saw it that way :-)</td>', 'Thanks, wish more people thougth/saw it that way :-)', '2005-11-30 07:32:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1906927, 260465, 44944, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your comments.<br/> <br/>A short explanation how I made this picture. I had a mirror lying on a table. Perpendicular I had a yellow sheet of paper which I photographed via the mirror. This caused the yellow "background". On the mirror I positioned the three dice. Due to the thickness of the glass in the mirror the dice seemed to float. Finally I placed a center-image filter on my lens to produce the feathered look.<br/> <br/>Then it is time to take the picture, using a direct flash, resulting in two light spots on the dice (direct path and mirror-path).<br/> <br/>Kind regards</td>', 'Thank you all for your comments. A short explanation how I made this picture. I had a mirror lying on a table. Perpendicular I had a yellow sheet of paper which I photographed via the mirror. This caused the yellow "background". On the mirror I positioned the three dice. Due to the thickness of the glass in the mirror the dice seemed to float. Finally I placed a center-image filter on my lens to produce the feathered look. Then it is time to take the picture, using a direct flash, resulting in two light spots on the dice (direct path and mirror-path). Kind regards', '2005-11-30 07:54:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1906933, 260662, 11793, '<td valign="top">great ! - congrats<br/></td>', 'great ! - congrats', '2005-11-30 07:59:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(1907005, 260966, 11738, '<td valign="top">Way to go Samuel! Nonc Nis trouve que tu prends des belles photos pour un garçon de deux ans.<br/> <br/>To those who commented on this image, I guess some of you didn`t look closely enough.  The photographer is two years old.<img alt="'' . substr(''//www.talkfrontpage.com/images/smilies/eek.gif'', strrpos(''//www.talkfrontpage.com/images/smilies/eek.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.talkfrontpage.com/images/smilies/eek.gif"/> <br/> <br/>Hee hee!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-11-30 08:46:03.</i></td>', 'Way to go Samuel! Nonc Nis trouve que tu prends des belles photos pour un garçon de deux ans. To those who commented on this image, I guess some of you didn`t look closely enough.  The photographer is two years old.  Hee hee!', '2005-11-30 08:42:44.000000', '2005-11-30 08:46:03.000000', 0),
(1907029, 258910, 43869, '<td valign="top">Don''t beat yourself up lol.  I didn''t do so hot myself, my editing needs some SERIOUS help, plus one goose wasn''t as clear as the other- so I need focusing help also lol..<br/> <br/>I''m finding I''m doing much better with portrait type photos.   <br/> <br/>I like this though.  It''s very clear and the dof is good.  Better luck next time!</td>', 'Don''t beat yourself up lol.  I didn''t do so hot myself, my editing needs some SERIOUS help, plus one goose wasn''t as clear as the other- so I need focusing help also lol.. I''m finding I''m doing much better with portrait type photos.    I like this though.  It''s very clear and the dof is good.  Better luck next time!', '2005-11-30 08:55:15.000000', NULL, 0),
