(1907866, 260456, 40718, '<td valign="top">I think the composition of the photo is good.  Technically it isn''t bad.  The white of the yankee hat is quite blown and that immediately distracts.  I bet that cost you some.<br/> <br/>I have found many of these mediocre scoring photos lack contrast.  You were limited by your exposure, but the rest of the picture looks much better with an upping of +20 on your contrast.  Doing such blows the hat even more and also the baseball, so to get such you would need to reshoot the picture with a lower exposure. (or have wished for advanced editing)<br/> <br/>Finally, I bet the DNMC crowd bit you a bit. (you can see it in the 1-3 votes)  While I get what you are going for, it seems slightly shoehorned into the challenge.  I didn''t vote odd and I''m quite liberal in my threshold for meeting a challenge, but there are others that are very strict.  Whether you deserved it or not, I bet this lowered you by .1-.2.  The basketball just isn''t "odd" enough.  Yes, it isn''t baseball, but it is a sportsball, and in that respect they all go together.</td>', 'I think the composition of the photo is good.  Technically it isn''t bad.  The white of the yankee hat is quite blown and that immediately distracts.  I bet that cost you some. I have found many of these mediocre scoring photos lack contrast.  You were limited by your exposure, but the rest of the picture looks much better with an upping of +20 on your contrast.  Doing such blows the hat even more and also the baseball, so to get such you would need to reshoot the picture with a lower exposure. (or have wished for advanced editing) Finally, I bet the DNMC crowd bit you a bit. (you can see it in the 1-3 votes)  While I get what you are going for, it seems slightly shoehorned into the challenge.  I didn''t vote odd and I''m quite liberal in my threshold for meeting a challenge, but there are others that are very strict.  Whether you deserved it or not, I bet this lowered you by .1-.2.  The basketball just isn''t "odd" enough.  Yes, it isn''t baseball, but it is a sportsball, and in that respect they all go together.', '2005-11-30 14:29:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1907906, 259399, 40718, '<td valign="top">I actually like it.  I didn''t vote Odd, but I would have given it a 6 or 7.  Abstracts are tough on DPC and it seems like the only abstracts which survive are the ones which rely on a sharply focused pattern to gain its "abstractness" rather than using blur or DOF to become abstract.<br/> <br/>The dots which are either dirt or water on the bowl are a megadistraction.  I certainly would have knocked you for that.  They look like saturation artifact and as soon as I saw them, I would have either backed off on the saturation or reshot the pic.<br/> <br/>The colors are very pleasing and the fish is defined yet still abstract.  The final knock is the title.  Some people consider the title in their score and I think it''s a little off.  You ponder the title longer than the picture, and thus it is also a distraction.</td>', 'I actually like it.  I didn''t vote Odd, but I would have given it a 6 or 7.  Abstracts are tough on DPC and it seems like the only abstracts which survive are the ones which rely on a sharply focused pattern to gain its "abstractness" rather than using blur or DOF to become abstract. The dots which are either dirt or water on the bowl are a megadistraction.  I certainly would have knocked you for that.  They look like saturation artifact and as soon as I saw them, I would have either backed off on the saturation or reshot the pic. The colors are very pleasing and the fish is defined yet still abstract.  The final knock is the title.  Some people consider the title in their score and I think it''s a little off.  You ponder the title longer than the picture, and thus it is also a distraction.', '2005-11-30 14:37:00.000000', NULL, 0),
